        "mission_intent": "We need the internal controls team to build out a full enterprise risk management specification for our agency's financial reporting and improper payments compliance objectives, consistent with the framework outlined in OMB Circular A-123. Specifically, the spec should cover two risk scenarios: first, the material weakness identified in our internal controls affecting reliable external financial reporting, and second, the high susceptibility of Program X to significant improper payments under the improper payments legislation. For each scenario, document the inherent risk assessment using impact and likelihood dimensions (both starting at high), the risk response strategy (which should be reduction in both cases), the resulting residual assessment after corrective actions are applied (impact remaining high but likelihood reduced to medium), and the proposed corrective actions with designated owners. For the financial reporting objective, the CFO should own the corrective action involving technical assistance to program partners and ongoing monitoring in consultation with OMB to maintain our audit opinion. For the compliance objective, the Program Office should own the development of budget proposals to strengthen program integrity and ensure improper payment rates are actively monitored and reduced. Both scenarios should tie their proposed actions back to the Internal Control Assessment process, and the compliance objective should additionally reference the Strategic Review. Make sure the specification aligns risk analysis to the agency's strategic objectives as required under OMB Circular A-11, Section 230. We need this ready for senior leadership review by end of next quarter so we can incorporate it into our annual assurance statement.",
